/*
 * Per-hull slot layout — the core, hardpoint, utility and optional-internal mounts
 * every ship hull offers — keyed by the same Frontier `symbol` as
 * data/ships/ships.jsonc. Join the two on `symbol`.
 *
 * Source:  EDCD/coriolis-data, ships/*.json slots + bulkheads (commit 0db9234b5b9ce8c939ea84133d7ce336eea88e27)
 *          https://github.com/EDCD/coriolis-data
 *          The layout is Elite Dangerous game data, property of Frontier Developments
 *          plc, redistributed under Frontier's media-usage terms:
 *          https://forums.frontier.co.uk/threads/510879/
 *
 * `core` gives the size of each of the seven fixed core slots. `hardpoints` lists
 * the weapon-mount sizes (1 Small – 4 Huge). `utility` counts the tiny utility
 * mounts. `optional` lists the optional-internal slots in descending size, each with
 * an optional `restriction` ("military" or "planetaryApproachSuite"). `bulkheads`
 * carries the five armour options' added mass (t), for computing armour mass.
 * Present only where coriolis carries the hull (47/48).
 *
 * Full provenance: data/ships/SOURCES.md.
 */
